preConditionHook:
// BROOKS'S "TWENTY GAP BARS": the market has gone gapBarsRequired consecutive
// bars without a single bar touching the EMA -- a strong trend, and an overdone
// one. One PERSISTENT counter that resets whenever a bar's range straddles the
// average, tested against a threshold; the four restatements that spell it as a
// fixed-length loop over the EmaGapBar primitive cost a 20-deep loop and an EMA
// read per bar for the same bars, so the counter form wins.
//
// Not EmaGapBar, which is the ONE-BAR test and says nothing about how long the
// gap has run; not EmaTouch, which is the straddle itself. Nothing in the
// catalog carries a bars-since-event counter -- MomentumConsecutiveBars is the
// closest shape but counts a price relation over a fixed window, not a
// reset-on-event streak.
//
// DIRECTION-AGNOSTIC, deliberately: the counter does not care which side of the
// average the run is on, so both sides are identical text and a pane that wants
// the direction ANDs EmaGapBar or CloseBeyondEma. That differs from the mirrored
// loop forms only when price gaps clean across the average without any bar
// straddling it -- rare, and the price of the cheaper machine.
//
// Brooks says outright that twenty "is arbitrary ... any large number of bars",
// so gapBarsRequired is an optimizer input and not a book constant.
//
// MultiWalk's WFSafe_Xaverage, which the EasyLanguage twin calls, MEASURED
// BIT-IDENTICAL to the plain XAverage built-in AT A FIXED LENGTH ((wf - xa)
// exactly 0 on all 17,785 bars of EL_XAverage_Probe.txt, @OJ 240min):
//   * SEED is the PRICE on the study's first calculated bar, ctx.CurrentBar()
//     == 1 -- not a length-term simple average, which is what most other
//     platforms do and what a textbook twin would write;
//   * ONE STATEMENT IN EL'S FORM, x + sf*(p - x), never sf*p + (1-sf)*x: the
//     two are algebraically identical and separate in floating point on 67% of
//     bars past 100. Do not re-associate it;
//   * NO WARM-UP HOLE: non-zero from bar 1 on every probed bar, so no
//     CurrentBar guard returning 0;
//   * AN EMA NEVER FORGETS ITS SEED, so Max Bars Back and the chart start are
//     part of the specification (~330 bars of memory);
//   * UNMEASURED: the walkforward LENGTH CHANGE the wrapper exists for. PIN
//     emaLength in the grid until it is measured.
//
// ONLY THE CURRENT EMA IS READ. gapCount is a local holding its own previous
// value across bars, which is not the lagged function read XAverage(...)[k] --
// that remains unmeasured, and no rule here depends on it.
//
// emaSf is a localVariables entry rather than a hook-scope const so the hooks
// survive a double placement; it is recomputed every bar from the raw input,
// because EL's Length slot is numeric and 2/(Length+1) is evaluated on the
// value passed.
//
// Deepest bar touched: 0.
emaSf = 2.0 / (emaLength + 1.0);
if (ctx.CurrentBar() == 1) {
    emaVal = close[0];
} else {
    emaVal = emaVal + emaSf * (close[0] - emaVal);
}
touched = el_le(low[0], emaVal) && el_ge(high[0], emaVal);
if (touched) {
    gapCount = 0;
} else {
    gapCount = gapCount + 1;
}
